{"Soundness": 3, "Presentation": 3, "Contribution": 3, "Rating": 8, "Confidence": 4, "Strengths": "The proposed DC-AE is simple yet effective.

The paper is well-written and easy to follow.

The authors have conducted extensive experiments to demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed method.", "Weaknesses": "The paper would be stronger if the authors could conduct experiments on the larger models such as LDCC256 and Diffusion-6B. The paper also lacks the ablation study, i.e., the authors have not conducted experiments using only one of the proposed methods, i.e., Residual Autoencoding or Decoupled High-Resolution Adaptation.", "Questions": "None"}
